  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nHuman Services Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nHuman Services Required Courses\nHUSV 1101\nSocial Change and Human Services\n4\nHUSV 2300\nCounseling in Human Services\n4\nHUSV 3570\nThe Nonprofit Sector, Philanthropy, and Social Change\n4\nHUSV 3900\nSocial Policy\n4\nHuman Services Electives\nComplete five additional HUSV courses.\n20\nSociology Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nRequired Sociology Courses\nSOCL 1101\nIntroduction to Sociology\n4\nSOCL 3300\nSocial Theory\n4\nIntroductory Electives\nComplete two courses between\nSOCL 1000\nand SOCL 2999 not used to satsify another requirement\n8\nIntermediate-Level Elective\nComplete two courses between SOCL 3000 and SOCL 4999 not used to satisfy another requirement\n8\nResearch Methods Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one required methods course, one required statistics course, and one qualitative methods course:\n12\nHUSV 2970\nResearch Methods for Human Services\nor\nSOCL 2321\nResearch Methods in Sociology\nor\nINSH 3101\nResearch Methods in the Social Sciences\nSOCL 2320\nStatistical Analysis in Sociology\nor\nINSH 3102\nIntroduction to Statistics in the Social Sciences\nor\nPOLS 2400\nQuantitative Techniques\nor\nCRIM 3700\nAnalyzing and Using Data on Crime and Justice\nSOCL 2323\nEthnographic Methods\nor\nANTH 3410\nEthnographic Field Experience\nHuman Services/Sociology Integrative Course\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one integrative course from the following list:\n4\nHUSV 2355\nRace, Identity, Social Change, and Empowerment\nANTH 3100\nGender, Social Justice, and Transnational Activism\nSOCL 3450\nClass, Power, and Social Change\nCapstone Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one capstone course from either department:\n4\nHUSV 4700\nSenior Seminar in Human Services\nSOCL 4600\nSenior Seminar\nSociology Major Grade Requirement\nA GPA of 2.000 for major courses is required.\nHuman Services and Sociology Combined Major Credit Requirement\nComplete 80 semester hours in the major.\nExperiential Liberal Arts\nAll students in this College of Social Sciences and Humanities program are required to complete the\nExperiential Liberal Arts Requirement\n.\nProgram Requirement\n128 total semester hours required",
